<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45442" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφροσύνη</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋφρ</span>-, ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔφρων</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mirth, merriment</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέλω τε καὶ εὐφροσύνην παρέχουσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				10.465
			</span></i>, etc.; esp. of a banquet, <i>good cheer, festivily</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ . . τί φημι χαριέστερον εἶναι ἢ
				ὅτ᾽ ἐϋφροσύνη μὲν ἔχῃ κατὰ δῆμον ἅπαντα
			κτλ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				9.6
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				449
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				482
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρατὴρ μεστὸς ἐϋφροσύνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					1.4
				</span></i>
			: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφισι θυμὸς αἰὲν
				ἐϋφροσυνῃσιν ἰαίνεται</span> is cheered <i>with glad
				thoughts</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.156
			</span></i>; <i>festivities</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				539
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				377
			</span></i> (both lyr.), etc.: chiefly poet., used by <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ages.</u>
				9.4
			</span></i> (pl.): in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.3.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				80b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ χαρὰ καὶ ἡ εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				2
			</span></i>: also in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				31.27
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				2.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diogenian.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				4.50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLips.</u>
				119 ii 1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ψυχῆς οἶνος πινόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Si.</u>
					34.28
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				31.36
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> pr. n.,
				<u>Euphrosyne</u>, one of the Graces, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				909
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
